# Data conversion between kilobyte and megabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between kilobyte and megabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1KB to 0.001MB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KB yields 0.0015MB; backward, converting 1MB to 1000KB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5MB yields 1500.0KB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1KB
print(forward_whole->to(MB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KB
print(forward_fractional->to(MB))
backward_whole: int = 1MB
print(backward_whole->to(KB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MB
print(backward_fractional->to(KB))

<<< stdout
0.001MB
0.0015MB
1000KB
1500.0KB

<<< stderr
